Evaluation output lands here.

Only runs with real providers are committed. A run on the fake embedding
provider uses random vectors, so its numbers measure nothing, and committing
them -- even carrying their disclaimer -- risks someone quoting a figure that
was never a result.

    python evaluation/run_experiments.py
    python evaluation/run_experiments.py --dataset evaluation/dataset_flask.json

The first writes experiments.json/.md, the second experiments_flask.json/.md.
The README results tables are filled in from these files.
